    "summary": "I built a three-storey drawer cabinet. It is three north-half hex bases stacked at cell (0,0), on levels 0, 1 and 2, joined by snaps. Each level has a drawer on its cut face, so there are three drawers, one above the other. A top cover closes the top. I ran capOpenFaces, which put solid caps on the open edges, and lockJoints. check_build found no rule issues and the mesh-collision check came back clear. The print budget is about 1849 g and 2676 minutes, for 34 parts. The build started with one full base, which had no drawer site, so I removed it to make room for the half bases. I added no props because the brief didn't ask for any.",
